    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The control this vendor deposit reconciliation needs",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Accounts Payable Manager treats vendor deposit reconciliation as a control problem rather than a speed problem. The work starts when a vendor deposit is applied to an order enters the vendor deposit reconciliation file, not when someone remembers to check it. A accounts payable specialist prepares the evidence, but the controller keeps the decision that changes money or access. The record should let a reviewer reconstruct the case without asking the person who did the work.",
          "A vendor deposit reconciliation queue is only useful when each item has an owner and a next action. Accounts Payable Manager asks the team to record a vendor deposit is applied to an order at the moment it arrives, not after the case has already moved. That habit keeps the queue honest when volume rises and the same person is covering two roles. A control that depends on memory fails quietly, and the failure usually appears in a later reconciliation."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "What the vendor deposit reconciliation record must show",
        "paragraphs": [
          "The evidence standard for vendor deposit reconciliation is deliberately modest. Record the deposit request and payment, the final invoice and order reference, and the application or refund record with the date each was observed. Mark a missing value as missing instead of filling it from memory. A later reviewer will treat an invented value as fact, and that is how a small gap becomes a control failure.",
          "Accounts Payable Manager keeps the original source and the correction note side by side for vendor deposit reconciliation. The file should show the deposit request and payment, the final invoice and order reference, and the application or refund record without requiring a second system login. A reviewer who has to reconstruct the source loses time and may accept a weaker record. The standard is not a perfect file; it is a file that makes the decision reviewable."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where the support role stops",
        "paragraphs": [
          "A accounts payable specialist should never be asked to guess what the controller would prefer on vendor deposit reconciliation. The role brief should name the decisions the specialist may complete and the decisions that always escalate. Accounts Payable Manager reviews that brief when a new exception type appears, not once a year. A clear boundary protects the specialist as much as it protects the ledger.",
          "The support role can prepare vendor deposit reconciliation, gather documents, and draft the note. It cannot approve a payment, release a bank change, or decide that an exception is safe. The controller owns those decisions, and the boundary should be written next to the queue. A verbal rule disappears when volume rises, so make the stop conditions explicit."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "The daily vendor deposit reconciliation routine",
        "paragraphs": [
          "The daily routine for vendor deposit reconciliation is short and repeatable. Start with the oldest open case, then match each item to its source record. Next, record every missing item and a deposit applied to a different order, and finally route the case to the controller. End the shift with a handoff that names what moved and what is still open.",
          "Accounts Payable Manager keeps the vendor deposit reconciliation queue small enough to finish. A queue that never empties hides its oldest item behind a healthy average. Each case gets one owner, one next action, and one review date. The next person should be able to continue without reconstructing the day."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Exceptions that should stop the case",
        "paragraphs": [
          "When a vendor deposit reconciliation exception is resolved, the note should say what changed and what would reopen it. A close that says only reviewed is not evidence. Accounts Payable Manager asks for the destination field that actually changed and the date it changed. That detail is what makes the next review faster.",
          "The most expensive vendor deposit reconciliation exception is the one that looks routine. Accounts Payable Manager treats a deposit applied to a different order as a stop condition until the controller confirms the right treatment. The case note should name the exception, the person who resolved it, and the evidence used. A pattern of the same exception is a signal to change the form or the rule, not to work faster."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "How to verify and close",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Accounts Payable Manager verifies vendor deposit reconciliation with the same questions every time. Did the record show the deposit request and payment and the application or refund record? Did the controller make the decision that apply, refund, or hold the deposit? If either answer is no, the case is not closed, even when the payment has already moved.",
          "Verification for vendor deposit reconciliation means checking that each case has a source, a business purpose, and an approval. A sent reminder or a closed ticket proves activity, not outcome. Accounts Payable Manager reviews a small sample against the same definition each month. The sample should include one difficult case, not only the easy queue."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "The weekly vendor deposit reconciliation handoff",
        "paragraphs": [
          "The weekly handoff for vendor deposit reconciliation belongs with the record, not in a private message. Name what moved, what stalled, and who owns the next check. Accounts Payable Manager asks the specialist to date the handoff and link it to the open case. A Monday reviewer should be able to continue without an interview.",
          "A good handoff also states what would reopen a closed vendor deposit reconciliation case. A late source, a vendor question, or a changed approval can all change the answer. Accounts Payable Manager records those triggers beside the close note. The next owner then knows whether to trust the record or reopen it."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "The monthly vendor deposit reconciliation review",
        "paragraphs": [
          "The monthly review should end with one process change and one owner. Accounts Payable Manager does not accept a review that ends with general encouragement. The team fixes the form, the source, or the queue rule, then checks the same measure next month. That rhythm turns vendor deposit reconciliation from a recurring complaint into a managed control.",
          "Accounts Payable Manager uses the monthly vendor deposit reconciliation review to test one assumption. Pick a case where a deposit can be paid twice or left unapplied, then trace the evidence back to the source. If the trace requires a private message, the record is not complete. The fix belongs in the form or the queue rule, not in a reminder to be more careful."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "What should the team check first on vendor deposit reconciliation?",
        "a": "Start with the source record and the named owner. Accounts Payable Manager asks the specialist to record the deposit request and payment and the application or refund record before the case moves forward, and the controller keeps the release decision."
      },
      {
        "q": "Which vendor deposit reconciliation decisions stay with the accountable owner?",
        "a": "The controller owns every decision that changes money, access, policy, or a vendor commitment. The specialist prepares the evidence and routes the exception instead of resolving it."
      },
      {
        "q": "How should vendor deposit reconciliation results be reviewed?",
        "a": "Review a small sample against the same definition each month. Accounts Payable Manager records the source, the decision, the close evidence, and one process change with an owner and a check date."
      }
    ],
